    "smsToSaturateHbm": {
      "value": 32,
      "unit": "count",
      "confidence": "estimated",
      "sources": [
        "Little's law: 3.35 TB/s × ~0.7 µs of loaded HBM latency (assumed; no cited H100 figure) ≈ 2.3 MB in flight. A pipelined GEMM or attention CTA keeps ~64–96 KB of TMA loads in flight (4–6 stages of ~16 KB), so ~24–36 SMs saturate HBM",
        "Answers brief §12's open question (do 32 CTAs saturate HBM?) as 'about' for pipelined kernels. Plain-load kernels need more SMs (Chips and Cheese, \"Nvidia's H100: Funny L2, and Tons of Bandwidth\": H100 PCIe leads A100 in VRAM bandwidth only 'if you can fill more than half the GPU'), but those kernels move little and are overhead-bound"
      ]
    },
